  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 73ff519377b990a4c81cd1461a3c1f62, type: 3}
  m_Name: Sally_W21_Teach
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogueNode
  speakerName: Sally
  speakerPortrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 7733d16353c0fcf4b99b8f89f3ad1780, type: 3}
  dialogueText: 'No makisabatka iti baro a tao, mabalinmo met a kayat a maammoan
    no sadino ti naggapuan na.


    Iti Ilokano, ti ''taga sadino ka?'' ket kayatna
    a saoen ti ''where are you from?''


    Usarem daytoy no damagem no sadino ti
    ili wenno lugar a naggapuanna.


    Denggem a naimbag: taga sadino ka?


    Ita,
    padasem nga ibagam ti ''taga sadino ka?'' iti bukodmo a timek.'
  translatedText: 'When meeting someone new, you may also want to learn where they
    come from.

    In Ilokano, ''taga sadino ka?'' means ''where are you from?''

    Use
    it when asking someone about their hometown or place of origin.

    Now, try
    saying ''taga sadino ka'' yourself.'
